# ======================================================================
# WHICH LEAGUES, IN ONE PLACE.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# There used to be two crontab lines, each carrying its own copy of these
# lists, and they DISAGREED:
#
#   10 8  * * *  LEAGUES="wnba nfl mlb mls"                        --build
#   0,30 8-23 *  LEAGUES="wnba nfl mlb mls" RUN_LEAGUES="wnba nfl"
#
# The build line named no RUN_LEAGUES, so start-slate.sh defaulted it to
# LEAGUES and the builder was told every league was hosted. The filter that
# keeps unhosted rooms off the player's rail was therefore INERT on the one
# line that actually builds the slate each morning — fifteen mute baseball
# rooms would have gone onto the rail at 08:10 on a game night, exactly the
# failure the filter was written to stop. It only ever worked when the
# morning build had failed and the self-heal ran it from the start line's
# environment instead.
#
# One fact, one file. The cron lines now name a schedule, not a policy.
# The environment still wins, so a hand run can still say
# `RUN_LEAGUES="wnba nfl mlb" host/start-slate.sh` for one evening.
# ======================================================================

# Built: schedule docs, rosters and question banks. Cheap — a few writes.
# Build wide: the data is what the backtest and tomorrow's decision run on.
LEAGUES="wnba nfl mlb mls"

# Hosted: a node process, a lease, and a feed poll every 30s for four hours.
# ALSO decides what the player's rail offers, because a room nobody hosts
# must never appear as a room. Turn a league on here, not in a cron line.
# 19 Aug: MLS added so Spanish can be tested against a soccer crowd, which
# is where it will actually matter. CURATED with host/pick-slate.sh, not
# left wide open — eleven MLS matches against MAX_ROOMS=2 would put nine
# mute rooms on the rail, which is the RUN_LEAGUES bug reappearing one
# level down. host/slate-offer.js keeps the rail equal to the manifest.
# 20 Aug: MLB added. Thursday is the first live BASEBALL room this product
# has ever opened — Nationals @ Rangers 5:05pm PT, then 49ers @ Chargers at
# 7:00pm, two hours apart so one person can settle into the ballgame and then
# switch to the football room mid-evening. That cross-sport switch against two
# real rooms is the point of the night.
#
# THIS LINE ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH AND MUST NOT BE READ AS ENOUGH. Baseball plays
# fifteen games a day and most of them start in the morning, so with the global
# MAX_ROOMS the early games take every slot hours before the two games above are
# due. The pick file is what makes the night the night:
#     ~/gamenight-logs/slate-pick-2026-08-20.txt
# It names the two rooms, it wins over this variable in both build-slate.js and
# start-slate.sh, and it survives the 08:10 rebuild. Turning a league on here
# WITHOUT one is how a day gets eleven rooms nobody is hosting.
RUN_LEAGUES="wnba nfl mlb mls"

# Most rooms live AT ONCE, across all leagues — not per league, not per day.
# The ceiling is Firestore reads, and it is lower than it looks:
#   runner alone            ~2,880 reads/room-night  ->  ~15 rooms/day
#   runner + watch-night.js ~5,610 reads/room-night  ->  ~8  rooms/day
# against a 50,000/day free tier that resets at midnight Pacific. When it
# runs out, claimLease throws, every runner dies at once, and every phone
# in every room stops together — including the flagship, killed by rooms
# nobody was sitting in. Raise this deliberately, with the watchdog in mind.
# 19 Aug: 2 -> 3. Three SLATE rooms tonight (Tempo@Mystics 4:30, LAFC@COL
# 6:30, SJ@LA 7:30) plus the flagship, which runs from its own cron line
# and does not spend a slot. At 2 the launcher would have started the two
# EARLIEST and silently refused SJ @ LA — the FS1 match — with nothing but
# a log line. Four concurrent rooms is ~27,400 Firestore reads, 55% of the
# free tier, against a measured ceiling of ~8 rooms with the watchdog on.
# This is also the first night four rooms have ever run at once: read
# SB.budget() from a phone console at full time and replace this estimate
# with a real number before 29 Aug.
MAX_ROOMS=3
